#### **3.2 Implement the TaskManager**
The `TaskManager` will serialize tasks and send them over the network using input/output streams.

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.net.Socket;
import java.util.List;

public class TaskManager {
    private Socket socket;
    private ObjectOutputStream out;
    private ObjectInputStream in;

    public TaskManager(Socket socket) throws IOException {
        this.socket = socket;
        this.out = new ObjectOutputStream(socket.getOutputStream());
        this.in = new ObjectInputStream(socket.getInputStream());
    }

    // Send tasks to the remote device
    public void sendTasks(List<Task> tasks) throws IOException {
        out.writeObject(tasks);
        out.flush();
    }

    // Receive tasks from the remote device
    public List<Task> receiveTasks() throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        return (List<Task>) in.readObject();
    }

    // Close the connection
    public void close() throws IOException {
        out.close();
        in.close();
        socket.close();
    }
}
