### Java Code:

```java
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.NodeList;
import org.w3c.dom.Node;
import org.w3c.dom.Element;
import java.io.ByteArrayInputStream;

public class XmlExtractor {

    public static String extractEmailById(String xmlString, String id) {
        try {
            // Convert the XML string to a ByteArrayInputStream
            ByteArrayInputStream input = new ByteArrayInputStream(xmlString.getBytes("UTF-8"));

            // Create a DocumentBuilderFactory and configure it
            DocumentBuilderFactory dbFactory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
            DocumentBuilder dBuilder = dbFactory.newDocumentBuilder();

            // Parse the XML string into a Document
            Document doc = dBuilder.parse(input);
            doc.getDocumentElement().normalize();

            // Get all user elements
            NodeList userList = doc.getElementsByTagName("user");

            // Iterate through user elements to find the one with the matching id
            for (int i = 0; i < userList.getLength(); i++) {
                Node userNode = userList.item(i);
                if (userNode.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
                    Element userElement = (Element) userNode;
                    if (userElement.getAttribute("id").equals(id)) {
                        // Get the email element
                        NodeList emailList = userElement.getElementsByTagName("email");
                        if (emailList != null && emailList.getLength() > 0) {
                            Node emailNode = emailList.item(0);
                            if (emailNode.getNodeType() == Node.ELEMENT_NODE) {
                                Element emailElement = (Element) emailNode;
                                return emailElement.getTextContent();
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
        return null; // Return null if no matching email is found
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String xmlString = "<root><user id=\"1\"><name>John Doe</name><email>john@example.com</email></user><user id=\"2\"><name>Jane Doe</name><email>jane@example.com</email></user></root>";
        String idToFind = "1";
        String extractedEmail = extractEmailById(xmlString, idToFind);
        System.out.println("Extracted Email: " + extractedEmail);
    }
}
```

### Explanation:
1. **Input Handling**: The XML string is converted into a `ByteArrayInputStream` for parsing.
2. **Parsing**: `DocumentBuilder` is used to parse the XML string into a `Document` object.
3. **Traversal**: The code traverses the XML DOM to find the `user` element with the specified `id`.
4. **Extraction**: Once the correct `user` element is found, it extracts the text content of the `email` element.
5. **Return**: The extracted email is returned as a string.

### Output:
For the given XML and `id="1"`, the output will be:
```
Extracted Email: john@example.com
